! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F204E "TEST NORMALIZATION
! MODIFIER" (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.65, octal 013041.00-
! 013103.40): six sub-tests of the NORMALIZED add to memory, M+(N).
!   E1-E3, E6: a flagged operand (XFP or XFN range) in memory and/or
!     the accumulator -- the normalization modifier is IGNORED and the
!     result is the dominating flagged operand unchanged (Ref. Manual
!     p.87 / Fig.23: XFP dominates N and XFN, N dominates XFN, equal
!     ranges take the algebraically larger exponent). "error if result
!     norm".
!   E4, E5: an N-range result (XFN + N, N + N) must come out
!     NORMALIZED and equal the pool constant (FPK6, FK44). "error if
!     result not norm".
! How each check works: CT0110(BU,60),ROS,4 compares ROS bits 0-59 with
! the accumulator field at offset 4 -- the RIGHT half's bits 0-59,
! which still hold the 64-bit copy the VFL L(BU) left there (an FP
! L(U) writes only the left half); E2/E3 reload it explicitly and
! E4/E5 load the expected constant. E6 uses offset 68 instead: the
! LEFT half's bits 0-59, i.e. the accumulator operand FK30 itself,
! which has the larger exponent of two XFN operands and so must be the
! result. So the block also pins the accumulator layout: a VFL load
! lands in the right half (bits 64-127 of the 128), an FP load in the
! left (bits 0-63), connective offsets count from the right end.
!
! Substitutions (SSIP framework, real listed addresses): SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch, ROS (octal 22355)
! the memory operand, PASS -> the routine's exit at 013103.40 (the
! listing's "B,$+1."). Constants from the pool pp.176-178. The entry
! FMA7's "BD,$+.32" is kept verbatim.
!
! Instructions: BD, L(BU)/ST(BU), L(U), M+(N), CT0110 with offsets 4
! and 68, SIC, BRGZ. verify_fp_arith_f204e_listing.py checks every
! word bit-for-bit.
!
! Observed: FIRST RUN HALTED AT SERS with SEN = 013070.40, sub-test
! E4's "error if result not norm", ROS holding FPK7 unchanged where
! FPK6 (FPK7 normalized: fraction up three places, exponent 3 -> 0)
! was expected. Cause: fpAdd's flagged-operand path returned the
! surviving operand with normalization suppressed in every case; that
! is right when the result is a FLAGGED operand (E1-E3, E6) but the
! survivor of XFN + N is the unflagged N operand, an ordinary number,
! and a normalized operation post-normalizes it. Fix: fpAdd normalizes
! an unflagged survivor when normalized operation is specified. After
! the fix all six sub-tests pass and the run halts at PASS with SEN
! still 0; E6 leaves ROS = FK30, the accumulator operand, as the
! larger-exponent XFN of the two. That first run is the discriminating
! evidence for this block.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0
        SLC, (8)22355.0
ROS     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool pp.176-178) --

        SLC, (8)22013.0
FPK6    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000125252525252525200
        SLC, (8)22014.0
FPK7    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001412525252525252520
        SLC, (8)22017.0
FPK10   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0002402525252525252520
        SLC, (8)22040.0
FPK27   DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777677777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22167.0
FK21    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777403777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22174.0
FK26    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777412525252525252520
        SLC, (8)22176.0
FK28    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031005252525252525240
        SLC, (8)22200.0
FK30    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577617777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22201.0
FK31    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777612525252525252520
        SLC, (8)22216.0
FK44    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000525252525252525000

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)13041.0
FMA7    BD, $+.32
        L(BU), FK21   ! F204E1: exp in XFP range
        ST(BU), ROS
        L(U), FK21   ! exp XFP range
        M+(N), ROS
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4   ! is norm modifier ignored
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS   ! error if result norm
        L(BU), FK26   ! F204E2: exp in XFP range
        ST(BU), ROS
        L(U), FK28   ! exp N range
        M+(N), ROS
        L(BU), FK26
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4   ! is norm modifier ignored
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS   ! error if result norm
        L(BU), FK26   ! F204E3: exp in XFP range
        ST(BU), ROS
        L(U), FK30   ! exp XFN range
        M+(N), ROS
        L(BU), FK26
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4   ! is norm modifier ignored
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS   ! error if result norm
        L(BU), FK31   ! F204E4: exp in XFN range
        ST(BU), ROS
        L(U), FPK7   ! exp N range
        M+(N), ROS
        L(BU), FPK6
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4   ! result should be norm
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS   ! error if result not norm
        L(BU), FPK10   ! F204E5: exp in N range
        ST(BU), ROS
        L(U), FPK10   ! exp N range
        M+(N), ROS
        L(BU), FK44
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS   ! error if result not norm
        L(BU), FPK27   ! F204E6: exp in XFN range
        ST(BU), ROS
        L(U), FK30   ! exp XFN range
        M+(N), ROS
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 68   ! is norm modifier ignored (vs the accumulator)
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS   ! error if result norm
PASS    BEW, $                  ! 013103.40: the routine's exit ("B,$+1.")
        END, FMA7
